# Baseline security headers for the static client.
#
# These have to live here rather than in the Worker: with no `run_worker_first` in
# wrangler.jsonc, Cloudflare's asset server answers /broadcast.html, /watch.html and
# /earthseed.js directly and the Worker never sees those requests. (The Worker sets the
# same headers on the responses it does serve, e.g. "/".)
#
# Still not a full CSP, but the reason has changed. The transport is now vendored, so there
# is no third-party script origin left to whitelist and `script-src 'self'` is finally the
# right shape. Two things remain before it can be enforced:
#   1. the inline <script type="importmap"> and inline module blocks in the two pages need
#      'sha256-…' hashes (and re-hashing whenever they change);
#   2. the AudioWorklet in earthseed.js is built from a blob: URL — allowing blob: in
#      script-src would undo much of the benefit, so that worklet should move to a real file.
# Do those, roll it as Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only, then enforce.
#
# What is here touches no script loading and so cannot break the app: clickjacking,
# MIME sniffing, base-tag hijacking, plugin embedding, referrer leakage.
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'none'; object-src 'none'
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
